---
# The bounds (one thread, one agent, one restart) end every behaviour
# with nothing left to do: that is rest, not a deadlock.
deadlock_detection: false
---

# A person's project session created while serve's running cap is full:
# it queues, and everything a person can do to the queued (then booting)
# row must work: open it, rename it, archive it, stop it, wait on it.
#
# Code: go/internal/serve/orbs.go createProjectSession (Main, then
# CreateChild with SpawnedBy=main, Thread=true); children.go CreateChild,
# launch, drainQueue, stopChild, busyChildren, queuedIDs/startingIDs;
# children_api.go createChild, queuedRow, pendingRows, childOf; api.go
# info/metaVerb (rename, archive, ack), getSession; web/src/app.tsx the
# transcript lookup's STARTING_MS window and start().
#
# The three entry points (palette 'New orb', the overview's project
# mode, the projects page's New session) are one POST /api/sessions
# {mode: project}; the server sees only whether it carries a prompt, so
# the spec has PostPrompt and PostEmpty. start() opens the new id at
# once, so both open it.
#
# Main(slug) runs first in the same handler; whether it had to create
# main is project_main_threads' flow and is folded into Post here. Main
# is a top-level session: it never sits in serve's running map.
#
# The cap: MAX_RUNNING = 1 slot, and the other occupant is main's own
# background agent (the model's tools.spawn), which is also what the
# per-session limit is for: MAX_PER_SESSION = 1 model agent. Every
# freed slot drains the queue in the same step (drainQueue runs from the
# event that freed it), as in background_agents.
#
# thread:
#   none      not posted yet
#   refused   the create answered 429 (the promise says never)
#   queued    meta.Task persisted, no process, no history file
#   booting   process started, holds the slot, no history file yet
#   empty     history written, no prompt, so no turn: its slot is free
#   running   history written, the prompt's turn open, holds the slot
#   idle      that turn closed
#   gone      a queued thread stopped: dropped with its row
# agent: none | running | queued | done (main's one model agent)
# view: what the open page shows for the thread: closed (not open),
#   queued, starting, transcript, missing ('Session not found')
# lastat: where the listed row's LastAt comes from: "post" (the create),
#   "history" (the file's last entry once it exists).
# verb: the answer to the last header verb on the row: "", ok, refused
#   (an error that says why), 404.
# spawn: "429" after main's model was refused an agent, until one ends.
#
# Where this disagrees with the code as of main 5471918e, the spec says
# what the flow promises and the code is the finding (stage 2 checks it):
#   - Open on a queued row: getSession 404s (a.info reads history only);
#     the page shows 'starting' for STARTING_MS (120 s) when it created
#     the id and then 'Session not found' while the list still shows the
#     row queued; opened from the list (not created by this page) it is
#     'Session not found' at once. Promised: 'queued', then 'starting'.
#   - queuedRow stamps Modified/LastAt = time.Now() on every read, so a
#     queued or booting row floats to the top and reads 'just now' for
#     as long as it waits. Promised: the create's time, stable.
#   - rename/archive/ack go through metaVerb, which 404s on any id with
#     no history file. Promised: rename works (meta only) and archive
#     refuses with a reason (409: stop it first) while the row is
#     pending. Ack is the same metaVerb path and is not modelled.
#   - CreateChild counts main's busy children (busyChildren) against
#     maxPerSession: a person's pending/running thread both takes a
#     model agent's budget and is itself refused (429) behind one.
#     Promised: only model agents count.
#   - A thread booting when serve restarts has had its Task cleared
#     (drainQueue saves before launch) and no history: after the restart
#     it is neither queued nor listed. Promised: it boots again.

MAX_RUNNING = 1
MAX_PER_SESSION = 1

PENDING = ("queued", "booting")
LIVE = ("empty", "running", "idle")
LISTED = ("queued", "booting", "empty", "running", "idle")
AGENT_BUSY = ("running", "queued")

def view_of(thread, opened):
    if not opened:
        return "closed"
    if thread == "queued":
        return "queued"
    if thread == "booting":
        return "starting"
    if thread in LIVE:
        return "transcript"
    return "missing"

role Queue:
    action Init:
        self.thread = "none"
        self.prompted = False
        self.agent = "none"
        self.spawn = ""
        self.opened = False
        self.view = "closed"
        self.lastat = ""
        self.renamed = False
        self.verb = ""
        self.restarts = 0

    # --- a person creates the session (either entry point), and the
    # page opens it at once. No per-session count applies to a thread.

    atomic action PostPrompt:
        require self.thread == "none"
        self.prompted = True
        self.lastat = "post"
        self.opened = True
        if self.agent == "running":
            self.thread = "queued"
        else:
            self.thread = "booting"
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    atomic action PostEmpty:
        require self.thread == "none"
        self.prompted = False
        self.lastat = "post"
        self.opened = True
        if self.agent == "running":
            self.thread = "queued"
        else:
            self.thread = "booting"
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    # --- main's model and its one background agent.

    atomic action AgentSpawn:
        # tools.spawn({background}) from main. Past its budget (model
        # agents only) 429 and nothing else changes; else it queues when
        # the slot is taken.
        require self.agent != "done" and self.spawn == ""
        agents = len([a for a in (self.agent,) if a in AGENT_BUSY])
        if agents >= MAX_PER_SESSION:
            self.spawn = "429"
        elif self.thread in ("booting", "running"):
            self.agent = "queued"
        else:
            self.agent = "running"

    atomic fair action AgentFinish:
        # The agent's turn closes; its slot drains the queue.
        require self.agent == "running"
        self.agent = "done"
        self.spawn = ""
        if self.thread == "queued":
            self.thread = "booting"
            self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    # --- the thread's own life.

    atomic fair action HistoryWritten:
        # The child's history file appears. With no prompt launch writes
        # none and gives the slot back, which drains a queued agent.
        require self.thread == "booting"
        self.lastat = "history"
        if self.prompted:
            self.thread = "running"
        else:
            self.thread = "empty"
            if self.agent == "queued":
                self.agent = "running"
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    atomic fair action Finish:
        require self.thread == "running"
        self.thread = "idle"
        if self.agent == "queued":
            self.agent = "running"

    # --- the page, and time passing on it.

    atomic action Poll:
        # The list's 4 s GET /api/sessions while the row is pending: it
        # must not move the row.
        require self.thread in PENDING
        pass

    atomic action StartingWindowExpires:
        # STARTING_MS (120 s) pass with the page on a pending id. A row
        # the list shows is still waiting, not missing.
        require self.opened and self.thread in PENDING
        pass

    atomic action Leave:
        require self.opened
        self.opened = False
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    atomic action Open:
        # Clicking the row in the list (a page that did not create it).
        require not self.opened and self.thread in LISTED
        self.opened = True
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    # --- header verbs on the pending row.

    atomic action Rename:
        # Meta only: a pending row has meta, so it takes the name.
        require self.thread in PENDING and not self.renamed
        self.renamed = True
        self.verb = "ok"

    atomic action Archive:
        # A pending row cannot be archived yet; serve says why (stop it).
        require self.thread in PENDING
        self.verb = "refused"

    atomic action Stop:
        # Stop agent on main's Work dialog: a queued child is dropped from
        # the queue and meta, so it has no row; an open page then shows
        # it missing, which is true.
        require self.thread == "queued"
        self.thread = "gone"
        self.verb = "ok"
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

    # --- serve restarts (launchd, bough update). Every child dies with
    # it: an open turn closes, and the running map starts empty, so what
    # was pending drains at once. Not with the agent queued: the restart
    # queue is ordered by id, which the spec cannot see.

    atomic action ServeRestart:
        require self.restarts == 0 and self.agent != "queued"
        self.restarts = 1
        if self.agent == "running":
            self.agent = "done"
            self.spawn = ""
        if self.thread == "queued":
            self.thread = "booting"
        elif self.thread == "running":
            self.thread = "idle"
        self.view = view_of(self.thread, self.opened)

action Init:
    queue = Queue()

# An id the list shows is never 'Session not found' by its own lookup.
always assertion ListedNeverMissing:
    return not (queue.view == "missing" and queue.thread in LISTED)

# A pending row's LastAt is the create's, however often the list polls.
always assertion PendingLastAtStable:
    return queue.thread not in PENDING or queue.lastat == "post"

# Every header verb on a listed row succeeds or says why; none 404s.
always assertion HeaderVerbsAnswer:
    return queue.verb != "404"

# A person's thread is never refused by, nor counted in, the model
# agents' per-session budget: a 429 means the model agents fill it.
always assertion ThreadOutsideAgentBudget:
    return queue.thread != "refused" and (queue.spawn != "429" or queue.agent in AGENT_BUSY)

# serve never runs more than its cap.
always assertion WithinCap:
    held = len([h for h in (queue.thread in ("booting", "running"), queue.agent == "running") if h])
    return held <= MAX_RUNNING

# A queued project session starts once a slot frees.
always eventually assertion QueuedStarts:
    return queue.thread != "queued"

# An opened pending session shows its transcript once it boots.
always eventually assertion OpenedBoots:
    return not (queue.opened and queue.thread in PENDING)
